IMPORT `lpa-special-provisions`

-- Liberty personal accident rules, UW-PAG-W-001-10-V: general provisions 7 (end of one
-- insured's cover), 8 (end of the contract), 9 (the short-period table) and 16 (premium
-- payment), src 1245-1435, 1536-1586.
--
-- Days are calendar days. "Within 30 days from day X" ends on day X + 30 (fork F35).

§ `16. Premium payment`

§§ `16A. The payment period`

-- It is a condition precedent to liability that every premium due is paid and received in
-- full: (a) within 30 days of the contract's effective date, or, if the period is under 30
-- days, within the period; (b) by instalments, if the Company agrees, the first within 30 days
-- of the effective date and the rest on the agreed dates, never for a period under 30 days;
-- (c) for an endorsement adding premium, within 30 days of its effective date, or within the
-- period if that is under 30 days. This is "Thời Hạn Thanh Toán", the payment period.
