GIVETH A NUMBER
`general provision 16A: the days to pay` MEANS 30

GIVEN `the effective date`              IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`general provision 16A: the last day of the payment period, effective` `the effective date` `, the period ending` `the last day of the period` MEANS
    IF   Day `the last day of the period` MINUS Day `the effective date` PLUS 1 LESS THAN `general provision 16A: the days to pay`
    THEN `the last day of the period`
    ELSE `the effective date` PLUS `general provision 16A: the days to pay`

GIVEN `the effective date`              IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`general provision 16A(b): instalments are possible, effective` `the effective date` `, the period ending` `the last day of the period` MEANS
    Day `the last day of the period` MINUS Day `the effective date` PLUS 1 AT LEAST `general provision 16A: the days to pay`

-- The duty, on a clock of days from the effective date (a period of 30 days or more).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `An actor` `An act`
`general provision 16A(a): the policyholder must pay the premium` MEANS
    PARTY  `the policyholder`
    MUST   `pay the premium due`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  FULFILLED
    LEST   BREACH BY `the policyholder`
           BECAUSE "general provision 16B: the premium was not paid in full within 30 days of the effective date, so the contract ends automatically from the next day"

§§ `16B. Automatic termination`

-- If the premium is not paid in full within the payment period, the contract or endorsement
-- ends automatically from the day after its last day, and the Company is free of every
-- liability arising from then. (a) The policyholder of the group still owes premium from the
-- start of the period to the termination, pro rata to the days in force over the days of the
-- period, even if no claim arose. (b) The policyholder must pay premium and receives the
-- benefit for an insured event between the start and the termination; for each insured the
-- premium is pro rata, and the most the insured receives is 0,1% of (i) the limit for each
-- benefit in the programme or (ii) the limit in the summary or endorsement for the claim,
-- whichever is less. The Company may deduct premium before paying.
