GIVEN `the premium for the whole period` IS A NUMBER
      `the first day of the period`      IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period`       IS A DATE
      `the day the contract ended`       IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`general provision 16B(a): the premium still owed, of` `the premium for the whole period` `for the period from` `the first day of the period` `to` `the last day of the period` `, ended on` `the day the contract ended` MEANS
    `the premium for the whole period`
    TIMES (Day `the day the contract ended` MINUS Day `the first day of the period`)
    DIVIDED BY (Day `the last day of the period` MINUS Day `the first day of the period` PLUS 1)

GIVETH A NUMBER
`general provision 16B(b): the fraction of the limit paid on an unpaid contract` MEANS 0.1%

GIVEN `the limit for the benefit in the programme` IS A NUMBER
      `the limit in the summary or endorsement`    IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`general provision 16B(b): the most paid on a claim, the programme limit being` `the limit for the benefit in the programme` `and the summary limit` `the limit in the summary or endorsement` MEANS
    `general provision 16B(b): the fraction of the limit paid on an unpaid contract`
    TIMES min `the limit for the benefit in the programme` `the limit in the summary or endorsement`

