GIVEN p IS AN `An insured person`
      g IS A `A ground for the end of cover`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`general provision 7: the ground carries a refund of premium, for` p `:` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `the insured ceased to be eligible` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the insured left Vietnam for over 180 consecutive days without notice or agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `employment with the employer ended` THEN
        CONSIDER p's `place in the group`
        WHEN `an employee of the employer` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `membership of the sponsoring organisation ended` THEN
        CONSIDER p's `place in the group`
        WHEN `a member of the sponsoring organisation` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    WHEN `the insured member's own cover ended` THEN
        CONSIDER p's `place in the group`
        WHEN `a dependant` r THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN p IS AN `An insured person`
      g IS A `A ground for the end of cover`
      `the annual premium`         IS A NUMBER
      `the premium paid`           IS A NUMBER
      `the first day of cover`     IS A DATE
      `the day cover ended`        IS A DATE
      `a claim was made, or the contract was breached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`general provision 7: the refund for` p `, ending on the ground` g `, annual premium` `the annual premium` `, paid` `the premium paid` `, cover from` `the first day of cover` `to` `the day cover ended` `, a claim or breach:` `a claim was made, or the contract was breached` MEANS
    IF       `general provision 7: the ground carries a refund of premium, for` p `:` g
         AND NOT `a claim was made, or the contract was breached`
    THEN max 0 (`the premium paid`
                MINUS `the annual premium` TIMES `general provision 9: the short-period rate, cover from` `the first day of cover` `to` `the day cover ended`)
    ELSE 0

§ `8. The end of the contract`

-- A. The contract ends: 8.1 when every insured's cover has ended; 8.2 by agreement; 8.3 by
-- cancellation, 8.4 by unilateral termination; 8.5 on the death or ineligibility of the
-- policyholder or an insured (for several insured, only that insured's part ends); 8.6 in other
-- cases the law provides. 8.1, 8.2, 8.5 and 8.6 state when the contract ends and turn on facts
-- the encoding takes as inputs (`date the group contract ended`, and general provision 7 for an
-- insured's part). Inert (src 1344-1347, 1403-1412).

§§ `8.3 Cancellation`

-- (a) restates Law 08/2022/QH15 art 22(1) (aid line 537-542). (b) If the policyholder
-- deliberately gives incomplete or false information (i) to make the contract and/or (ii) to be
-- paid, the Company may cancel; it pays nothing, refunds the premium less the costs of 8B, and
-- may set off the damages the policyholder owes, including benefits already paid. (c) If the
-- Company deliberately fails to inform or misinforms to make the contract, the policyholder may
-- cancel and recovers the premium paid. (d) The Company may cancel if a condition precedent is
-- not met. (e) Cancellation for fraud under general provision 5.
-- LAW: Law 08/2022/QH15 art 22(2) (aid line 543-547) gives the right to cancel for information
-- given in making the contract so as to be paid; 8.3(b) adds "và/hoặc (ii) để được bồi thường"
-- alone, information given only to be paid (fork F36: the document's wider ground is encoded).
