`general provision 8.3(c): the refund on cancellation for the Company's misinformation, premium` `the premium paid` MEANS
    `the premium paid`

§§ `8.4 Unilateral termination`

-- 8.4.1-8.4.2: where a change in the facts the premium rests on reduces the risk, the
-- policyholder may ask for (a) a lower premium, (b) a higher sum insured, (c) a longer period,
-- or (d) wider cover, and if the Company refuses, may terminate on immediate written notice.
-- 8.4.3-8.4.4: where it increases the risk (including a failure under general provision 6, a
-- change of occupation, or any illness or Injury arising in the period), the Company may
-- (a) recompute the premium, (b) reduce the sum insured, (c) shorten the period, or (d) narrow
-- the cover, and if the policyholder refuses, may terminate on written notice before
-- termination. 8.4.5: the Company may terminate if the premium is not paid in full by the
-- agreed time or after any grace period. These restate Law 08/2022/QH15 arts 23 and 26 (aid
-- line 560-587, 623-635).
